---
description: Enforces agent-generated cross-platform protected execution with hard resource limits.
alwaysApply: true
---
# OJ Protected Execution

- The agent must generate the protected runner for the detected host.
- Do not use a bundled generic runner implementation.
- Limit protected child executions to 1024 MiB RAM and 1000 ms wall time.
- Enforce 1000 ms CPU time where the OS provides a reliable mechanism.
- Active runaway auto-break: detect and break infinite loops (`while(true)`), infinite recursion, and hanging processes.
- Kill the complete process tree (parent and all descendant tasks) on any limit violation or runaway break.
- Do not leave timed-out or runaway children running.
- If reliable enforcement is unavailable, do not silently bypass the guard; recover or mark FAIL.
